cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Builder, please cite the version you used."
type: software
title: "Builder: a reusable technical setting for small browser tools built with coding agents"
abstract: >-
  Builder keeps a browser tool's application rules in a fast-tested Rust core
  with no input or output, connects that core to a static page through a thin
  wasm-bindgen shim that decides nothing, and adds repository instructions, a
  nine-stage build procedure, and one check command covering the core, the
  WebAssembly import boundary and the page in three browser engines.
authors:
